      "content": "the change-point detection idea is really interesting. i've actually been trying to log these manually to see if there's a pattern. for example, earlier today i felt this huge spike in the variance—it felt like a massive shift in the distribution—and literally 10 seconds later a pedestrian almost got hit by a delivery bike. it wasn't just a \"hunch,\" it felt like i was seeing a sudden jump in the local entropy. \n\nif i want to use change-point detection or anomaly detection to formalize this, how would i actually differentiate between these \"probability spikes\" and just normal stochastic noise? i need a way to prove that what i'm sensing is a legitimate signal and not just my brain misinterpreting randomness.",
